## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to reason about secret management granularity, cache invalidation, and zero-downtime refresh.

## Key Concepts

- Secrets mounted as files via projected volumes
- In-app credential caching and refresh patterns
- Signals and inotify/fsnotify for reload
- Rolling updates vs hot reload

## Code Example

```javascript
// Node.js snippet: watch credential file and reload
const fs=require('fs');
let creds;
function load(){
  creds = fs.readFileSync('/var/secrets/db-creds','utf8');
}
load();
fs.watch('/var/secrets/db-creds',(ev, f)=>{ if(ev==='change'){ load(); /* refresh DB pool here */ }});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you implement a Kubernetes-native approach to trigger a reload when secret rotates without application changes?
- What are trade-offs between in-pod reload vs restart and how to monitor?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes depth in cluster HA, RBAC, network isolation, and safe canary deployments under real-world constraints.

## Key Concepts
- HA control plane architecture across AZs
- etcd backup strategy and retention
- Namespace-scoped RBAC with Roles/Bindings
- NetworkPolicy-based tenant isolation (Calico or equivalent)
- Canary deployments and automated rollbacks with monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo canary rollout helper
async function canaryRollout(service, version, pct){
  // shift traffic
  await shiftTraffic(service, version, pct);
  // health check
  const ok = await checkHealth(service);
  if (!ok) await rollback(service, version);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure canary success and rollback safety at scale?
- How would you evolve RBAC and namespace isolation as tenants grow?
